      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "BACKGROUND",
          "Label": "CONTEXT",
          "content": "Exercise-related medial leg pain (ERMLP) is a common complaint among athletes, and efforts toward rehabilitation are often unsuccessful."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "OBJECTIVE",
          "content": "To evaluate the efficacy of a therapeutic intervention in ERMLP localized to soft tissue."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "DESIGN",
          "content": "A quasi-experimental, nonequivalent control-group study."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "SETTING",
          "content": "Athletic training facility."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "PATIENTS",
          "content": "20 volunteer male and female athletes (18-22 y old) with ERMLP. Complete data were available for 13 participants."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "INTERVENTION",
          "content": "Treatment group (TRE, n = 7) received therapeutic intervention focused on relieving muscle hypertonicity in the deep compartment of the lower leg and restoring balance of the toe flexors and extensors. Control group (CON, n = 6) received no intervention."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "MAIN OUTCOME MEASURES",
          "content": "Self-reported pain intensity, pain threshold, and extensor hallucis longus to extensor digitorum brevis (EHL:EDB) electromyography ratio."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "There were no significant differences in age, duration of symptoms, or pain measures between the 2 groups at baseline. CON demonstrated no significant changes in any of the outcome measures in posttreatment testing, but significant between-groups differences were identified for pain during activity (CON mean = 6.5, 95% CI 5.05, 7.95; TRE mean = 3.5, 95% CI 1.67, 5.33; P = .01), change scores for pain during activity (CON mean = 0.33, 95% CI -1.25, 1.91; TRE mean = -3.43, 95% CI:-4.6, -2.25; P < .001), change scores in pressure threshold (CON mean = -0.25, 95% CI -0.74, 0.23; TRE mean = 0.72, 95% CI 0.22, 1.37; P = .006), and change in EHL:EDB ratios (CON mean = 0.05, 95% CI -0.22, 0.33; TRE mean = 1.07, 95% CI 0.75, 2.07; P < .046)."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSION",
          "content": "Therapeutic interventions focused on restoring muscle balance appear to be effective in resolving ERMLP."
        }
      ]},
